    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_abstract_lattice_function" kindref="compound">AbstractLatticeFunction</ref> - This class is implemented by the dataflow instance to specify what the lattice values are and how they handle merges etc. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This gives the client the power to compute lattice values from instructions, constants, etc. The current requirement is that lattice values must be copyable. At the moment, nothing tries to avoid copying. Additionally, lattice keys must be able to be used as keys of a mapping data structure. Internally, the generic solver currently uses a <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_dense_map" kindref="compound">DenseMap</ref> to map lattice keys to lattice values. If the lattice key is a non-standard type, a specialization of <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_dense_map_info" kindref="compound">DenseMapInfo</ref> must be provided. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
